==Trivia==
*Aku Gory's Japanese name, Hellgoriller (ヘルゴリラー ''Herugorirā''), is likely a reference to the ''Dragon Quest'' monster [[wikia:dragonquest:Barbatos|Barbatos]], a bulky blue gargoyle-like demon who is known as Hellbattler (ヘルバトラー ''Herubatorā'') in Japan. ''Gorilla'' written in katakana would normally just be ゴリラ, without the ー (''[[wikipedia:Chōonpu|chōonpu]]''); the ''chōonpu'' is what turns it into Hellgoriller/Hellgorillaa.
*His description confirms that he used to be an [[Angelic Gory]] but got fired due to multiple mistakes. He can thus be considered a "Fallen Angel", which is the origin of [[wikipedia:Satan|Satan]] in Catholicism.
*The Aku Vortex mentioned in his description may be [[Aku Cyclone]] or the vortex-like portal that appears as [[The Aku Realms]]' menu button.
*His Japanese description saying he was fired for a dark business problem but came back as a video streamer seems to reference [[wikipedia:Hiroyuki Miyasako|Hiroyuki Miyasako]], who, along with several other comedians, temporarily lost his job soon after he was found to have been attending yakuza parties, but later resurfaced as a regular [https://youtube.com/channel/UCtubooLn_qgqoWsWS-UWuHw YouTuber]. This scandal has been dubbed お笑い芸人による闇営業問題 (roughly translated as "[[wikipedia:ja:お笑い芸人による闇営業問題|the comedians' dark business problem]]").
*He was technically an event enemy for a short time, as he was initially exclusive to the [[Empress' Research]] stages and [[Wrath of Hell (Deadly)|The Great Diablo]].
*He is the only [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemy to appear in a [[Main Chapters Levels|Main Chapter]] other than [[The Aku Realms]], appearing in [[Cats of the Cosmos]] Chapter 3 [[Gorigori (Cats of the Cosmos)/Outbreak|Gorigori]]'s [[Zombie Outbreaks|Zombie Outbreak]].

